t":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" block)."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","type":"heading","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Flag, don’t fake","type":"heading","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Beats","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Interaction","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction"}]},{"text":" patch.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"title":"Swami","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"},"do